atrix, replace the second column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(0+6)-(-5-0)+0 \\\\  & =18+5 \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{23}{-21}=-\\frac{23}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534256 17592186045417 true] [17592186416304 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416299 13194139534256 17592186045417 true] [17592186416304 1069 "q-42673" 13194139534256 17592186045417 true] [17592186416304 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534256 17592186045417 true] [17592186416304 1071 "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+y=-3 \\\\ x-3y-2z=4 \\\\ -2x+y+2z=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-14,$ then $z=$" 13194139534256 17592186045417 true] [17592186416304 1072 #uuid "4a38bcb4-0b4c-5b8b-bb9c-b7e3ce5c912c" 13194139534256 17592186045417 true] [17592186416304 1074 "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+1y+0z=-3 \\\\ 1x+(-3)y+(-2)z=4 \\\\ (-2)x+1y+2z=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+(-3)\